{"agent_id":"6Vw9","agent_seq":194,"timestamp":"2026-08-19T12:46:11.407594026Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"6095bfc0-16ac-4f7f-9da5-9a2845751d1f","title":"Make MCP resource capability requirements transport-specific","description":"S-019 follow-up for S-064/S-066. The list_mcp_resources and read_mcp_resource handlers currently declare REQUIRES_PROCESS_AND_NETWORK unconditionally. Stdio MCP needs Process while HTTP MCP needs Network, so a least-privilege run with only the transport it actually uses is rejected before the owned manager can select/revalidate the server transport. Model the requirement from the selected server/transport generation, fail closed for missing transport metadata, and add stdio-only, HTTP-only, mismatched, stale-generation, and mixed-server tests. Discovered during #1025; intentionally not widened into S-019 because the current rule is conservative and S-066 owns transport-specific admission.","priority":"medium","created_by":"6Vw9"},"signed_by":"SHA256:j+T69HS/M0AwPawKX5c+EFy9FaQnZPkMoDhPY7douB4","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg3hUp0i9PNKQQMq2guEzD3AVit1zRcPhExHUTd0ybTloAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKgJa2NMI5ZFtCf6FEGlBNB05pzYuoAxyZLc5xqkbiDJS8n85pOuyY5UBA8r1MsX96wGKRECRlLAKjZ0vCdCwwU="}
