{"agent_id":"6Vw9","agent_seq":616,"timestamp":"2026-08-21T07:54:59.159988473Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"706dcde7-cad4-4d11-b9bd-ee4d23d4158f","comment_uuid":"4d984301-d470-471b-b900-1366f85c52d3","author":"6Vw9","content":"S-003 architecture decision: replace all nine standalone fuzz bodies with calls into one normal Rust fuzz-harness library so the exact logic is unit-testable on the pinned Rust 1.98 toolchain. Arbitrary bytes are capped before parsing. Cron and hook targets call pure production validators; tool-argument fuzzing calls the mandatory effect classifier and never dispatches; path fuzzing uses an explicit process/network/secret-denied ToolRunContext rooted in owned TempDir state; provider/SSE/conversion targets assert deterministic bounded semantic state; streaming Markdown renders through an injected bounded in-memory writer with an explicit theme/width and is compared whole-vs-partitioned. Track curated seed-* corpus files while ignoring runtime-generated corpus hashes, and add CI checks for the separate fuzz crate. Rejected alternative: keep public execute_tool calls behind permissive/fake policy, because that still exercises effectful handler code and makes absence of host process/network/database effects an assumption rather than a type/call-boundary fact. VDD receipt remains queued until S-088.","created_at":"2026-08-21T07:54:59.157498413Z","kind":"decision","signed_by":"SHA256:j+T69HS/M0AwPawKX5c+EFy9FaQnZPkMoDhPY7douB4","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg3hUp0i9PNKQQMq2guEzD3AVit1zRcPhExHUTd0ybTloAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAdts/eNwAB6/21XgNLgJ+EbXPUwibsZ6bReEJPQsK3iH+YKlTp/t2uqYDAqCpvvd0BflDfSGK/vEd6CN3vLEfBg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:j+T69HS/M0AwPawKX5c+EFy9FaQnZPkMoDhPY7douB4","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg3hUp0i9PNKQQMq2guEzD3AVit1zRcPhExHUTd0ybTloAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIoQLpzS