{"agent_id":"6Vw9","agent_seq":667,"timestamp":"2026-08-21T10:15:51.098473213Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"b4d2a6bf-17e9-4d24-95f2-f47395504b83","comment_uuid":"67dcbb5e-b6d9-4707-b476-3c4d8b314e7d","author":"6Vw9","content":"S-012 architecture decision after production-call inventory: use a hybrid explicit-composition design, not a giant service-locator. ServiceRegistry will become a validated immutable lifecycle catalog plus the genuinely injected analytics sink; production constructors will have no Default/no-op fallback. Existing typed handles remain explicit at their consumers (PluginManager/McpManager, MemoryDb, guardrails, policy, ToolExecutor), and the catalog records their exact construction/consumer/shutdown anchors. The proxy compaction path will consume AutoCompactor so that policy seam is real. Generic OPENCLAUDIA_FEATURE_* values and configured team_memory_path will fail visibly while their implementations remain preserved for later typed-rollout and memory-identity slices. Unsafe background/plugin jobs, LSP staging, shadow PluginMcpRegistry, and rate-limit mock will be explicitly unavailable/experimental/test-only with follow-up slices rather than started or deleted. Credible alternative rejected: putting every heterogeneous handle behind ServiceRegistry would obscure capabilities/lifetimes, duplicate existing owners, and make run/session rebinding less type-safe. Capability registry gains an internal partial reachability record linked by tests to the lifecycle catalog; generation/projection evidence will be updated without promoting underlying services. VDD remains pending S-088.","created_at":"2026-08-21T10:15:51.095988138Z","kind":"decision","signed_by":"SHA256:j+T69HS/M0AwPawKX5c+EFy9FaQnZPkMoDhPY7douB4","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg3hUp0i9PNKQQMq2guEzD3AVit1zRcPhExHUTd0ybTloAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA+L7T3zPgvzX/movE9gEGVgX+C9ohYA6RXYIiWcEVdsrMEKidR64v